# state: any   (composed from the kept profile's survey shots; lane.zetaroutes1012)
# titlestate.admit() refuses `returning` for this golden: ab037a065b15 is
# title data only, no save directory (confirmed by the boot table below --
# MAIN MENU still defaults to NEW GAME highlighted, no LOAD GAME taken, no
# save-name screen). `any` is what the gate names for a route confirmed on
# a data-only golden as-is; this file keeps its required name
# (ninja-gaiden-black.returning.route) but is loaded with `# state: any`.
# Ninja Gaiden Black (5443000D), Nova, kept profile golden ab037a065b15.
# Boot and menu cadence read from the survey run z-1791797921-fpsbelow1012-1777822
# (survey.route, HAKUX_ZETA_D24=1); table in docs/lanes/zetaroutes1012/NOTES.md
# section 3. That run's own START/A spam (5s cadence) produced this screen
# sequence on the kept-profile disk:
#   025434-booted: title card, "PRESS START BUTTON".
#   025441 (START): MAIN MENU, NEW GAME already highlighted (same default as a
#     fresh disk -- this title's kept profile does not change the menu default).
#   025447 (A): narrative cutscene begins, "A legendary sword," sword close-up.
#   025452..025717 (12 more START/A cycles): the same long narrative/story-text
#     sequence belowbar1005/routes/bb-ngb.route documents step by step (steps
#     6-27: "The Book of the Fiends", "The Dark Dragon, now full of evil
#     intent, joined with Vigoor...") -- text-identical on this kept-profile
#     disk, so bb-ngb.route's own per-step press/wait cadence is reused
#     verbatim below rather than re-deriving it from the survey's coarser 5s
#     cycling.
#   025742-play: CHAPTER 1 "The Way of the Ninja", a blue "Proceed" prompt --
#     bb-ngb.route's own comment for this screen says the recorded path needed
#     `press X`, but the survey's generic loop (bare `press A`) ALSO cleared
#     it, into live gameplay. bb-ngb.route's `press X` (step 28) is still used
#     below since it's the one device-confirmed way past this screen; A is not
#     relied on here since bb-ngb.route documents X and a mixed route is not
#     needed.
#   025808 onward: live gameplay, Ryu over a fallen enemy by a waterfall, HUD
#     visible. The survey's own generic play loop (axis LY cycling + bare A +
#     RX swing) then leaves Ryu pinned against cave-wall geometry for the rest
#     of its ~4-minute window -- never visibly moving. So the play loop below
#     is bb-ngb.route's own "genre loop" (its lines 184-212, built from an
#     actual recorded playthrough alternating LY min/max with X/A/B presses and
#     RX swings), not the survey's loop.
# First run (z-1791820279-lane.zetaroutes1012-2514939, --seconds 900) reached
# moving play cleanly (fps_ok=0.9956, static_frac=0.0216) but FAILed on
# duration alone: 11 outer repeats of the genre loop run ~43s each (~481s of
# scripted movement), and the ~314s of boot/menu/cutscene cadence above the
# mark left only ~590s before the 900s request ran out -- 10s short of the
# 600s confirmation bar. The outer repeat count below is raised from 11 to 15
# (~650s of scripted movement) so the loop itself, not an idle post-script
# hold, covers the whole required window; the request's --seconds is raised
# to match.
